esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/join/LookupJoin.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/join/LookupJoin.java--1353:1382","promptId":"#NMZGT","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/join/LookupJoin.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/join/LookupJoin.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":1353,"endPos":1382,"startLine":30,"startLineOffset":70,"endLine":30,"endLineOffset":99,"length":30}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/join/LookupJoin.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/join/LookupJoin.java--2947:4232","promptId":"#4C8YZ","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/join/LookupJoin.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/join/LookupJoin.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":2947,"endPos":4232,"startLine":80,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":105,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1286}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":702,"line":710,"comment_lines":["[575][710]"],"review_comment":["Sorry, one last test suggestion - we can also add this in a separate PR if you\u0027re already about to make this ready to merge.\r\n\r\nI just noticed: all of the fls test cases have permission to read the `value` field, which is the join key.\r\n\r\nI think it\u0027d be interesting to test if forbidding this field for a user makes it so all look ups are null. And, if we wanna be extra paranoid, consider the case where the lookup index has duplicates for a given join key, so the `LOOKUP JOIN` would lead to extra rows - but without permissions granted on the join key, no extra rows should be emitted. (Otherwise, users could exfiltrate statistics about fields they have no permissions on).","Thanks Alex, I still have a couple of things to push, I\u0027ll add this one as well.\r\nI _think_ the whole query will fail because the user doesn\u0027t see the join key in the schema, but I\u0027ll double-check","The new tests confirm the above: if a role cannot see the join key in the lookup index, the query will fail with \"Unknown column\""],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/qa/security/src/javaRestTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/EsqlSecurityIT.java","id":37250,"created_at":"2025-01-24T09:51:43Z","original_position":36,"side":"RIGHT","position":187,"submitted_on_commit":"72328a1981c4b6cf505e54036912316eb7d09202","diff_hunk":"@@ -674,6 +685,20 @@ public void testLookupJoinFieldLevelSecurity() throws Exception {\n             )\n \n         );\n+\n+        resp \u003d runESQLCommand(\"fls_user4\", \"ROW x \u003d 40.0 | EVAL value \u003d x | LOOKUP JOIN `lookup-user2` ON value\");\n+        assertOK(resp);\n+        respMap \u003d entityAsMap(resp);\n+        assertThat(\n+            respMap.get(\"columns\"),\n+            equalTo(\n+                List.of(\n+                    Map.of(\"name\", \"x\", \"type\", \"double\"),\n+                    Map.of(\"name\", \"value\", \"type\", \"double\"),\n+                    Map.of(\"name\", \"org\", \"type\", \"keyword\")\n+                )\n+            )\n+        );\n     }","submitted_line":702},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The addition of new users (`fls_user2`, `fls_user3`, `dls_user`, `dls_user2`, `dls_user3`) and the method `createMultiRoleUsers` to create multi-role users is clear. However, there are some repetitive patterns in the user creation that could be refactored for better maintainability.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/qa/security/src/javaRestTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/EsqlSecurityIT.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/qa/security/src/javaRestTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/EsqlSecurityIT.java--30369:32286","promptId":"#5KG2C","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/qa/security/src/javaRestTest/java